--- body ---
## Context

0201 tracks the §2 quality "Coherence" axis. The per-field indicators are
landing piecemeal: `coherence_vocab_adherence`, `coherence_status_vocab_adherence`,
`coherence_capacity_nonnegative` (PR #651), and `coherence_row_atomicity` (0396).
Each is a per-run fraction = a diagnostic breakdown.

This ticket adds the layer *above* them: two **reference-free composite** scores
the author specified —

- **`coherence_internal`** — verifiable from the response alone.
- **`coherence_external`** — verifiable against world knowledge, *not* gold.

Their value: in production (PyPSA-ASEAN consolidation) there is no gold, so these
are the only quality signal available. Coherence ⟂ F1 — a model can be 100%
coherent yet 0% accurate; coherence is necessary, not sufficient, for accuracy.

## Design (locked with author)

**Aggregation: per-row pass/fail.** A row is internally coherent iff it passes
*all* internal checks; `coherence_internal = (fully-internal rows) / n_rows`.
Same for external. Rationale: the per-field signals are correlated (a merged
1NF row also has doubled, often out-of-band capacity); per-row pass/fail counts
such a row once per composite instead of double-penalising it. The per-field
fractions are kept as the diagnostic breakdown beneath the two scalars (ADR-7,
the #651 keep-fields-distinct precedent). The composites are therefore *stricter*
than any single adherence fraction (≈ product of pass rates) — document this so
they are not mistaken for the per-field numbers.

**Internal composite — per-row AND of:**
- fuel ∈ allowed vocabulary (reuse `_ALLOWED_FUELS`)
- status ∈ allowed vocabulary (reuse `_ALLOWED_STATUSES`)
- row is 1NF-atomic — **reuse 0396's per-row predicate; do not re-specify the
  detector here** (0396 owns the 14%→2.6% tightening and the false-positive
  exclusions). This ticket only needs 0396 to expose a row-level boolean, not
  just the run fraction.
- capacity numeric and ≥ 0 (reuse `_capacity_nonnegative`)

**External composite — per-row AND of:**
- province ∈ gazetteer (reuse `_province_known` from `coherence.py`; promote it
  to a scored column with `_annotation`)
- capacity ≥ 30 MWe and numeric. Lower bound 30 = task-scope compliance (the
  prompt asked for >30 MWe; a sub-30 row is out-of-requested-scope). **No flat
  upper band.** The Imagine-session verification killed the [30,1600] idea: a
  flat ceiling is meaningless because capacity plausibility is *level-conditional*
  (operating centrales max ≈1500 MW, but reference power-centers legitimately
  reach 6000 MW). The level-conditioned upper-plausibility check is a separate,
  richer signal that lives in 0402 (needs the `level` schema field from 0401);
  do not put a flat ceiling here.

Both composites land as per-run scalars in `records_to_metrics()` (ADR-7) and as
`coherence_*` columns (+ `_annotation`), threaded through scorer → mart → views
like their per-field predecessors.

## Two objectives — do not conflate

The internal composite treats a 1NF-violating row as a defect because this score
serves the **reference-free** objective. The matcher (0393) serves the
**reference-based** objective, where a merged "Cẩm Phả I & II" is decomposed and
matched (fabricates nothing) and is NOT a defect. Do not import either reading
into the other. See docs/inventory-1nf-handoff-exp2.md §Two objectives.

## First failing test

`tests/test_score_coherence.py` (red→green):
- `{"name":"Nhơn Trạch 3 & 4","fuel":"gas","status":"operating",
  "capacity_mwe":1200,"province":"Đồng Nai"}` → fails internal (non-atomic),
  passes external.
- `{"name":"Hà Tĩnh","fuel":"coal","status":"operating","capacity_mwe":12,
  "province":"Hà Tĩnh"}` → fails external (below the 30 MWe task scope), passes
  internal.
- `{"name":"Hà Tĩnh","fuel":"coal","status":"operating","capacity_mwe":600,
  "province":"Hà Tĩnh"}` → passes both → both composites = 1.0 on a singleton.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] `coherence_internal` and `coherence_external` emitted per run as per-row
      pass/fail fractions, alongside (not replacing) the per-field indicators.
- [ ] Internal AND includes 0396's per-row atomicity predicate (consumed, not
      re-implemented); external AND includes a new `coherence_province_known`
      column and a capacity ≥30-and-numeric check (no flat upper band).
- [ ] Both composites in `records_to_metrics()` (ADR-7); per-field breakdown
      retained.
- [ ] `tests/test_score_coherence.py` green; `make check` passes.
- [ ] Mart/view schema accepts the new columns (defensive `.get` per #651);
      real regen is out of scope → 0387.

## Out of scope
- The 1NF detector itself → 0396 (prerequisite).
- "Confidence vs number of sources" consistency check → v2; `confidence`,
  `sources[]`, `evidence_score` are not emitted at extraction today (needs a
  prompt+schema ticket first).
- Mart regeneration with the new columns → 0387 (needs-human, full-data env).
- Spider figure axis change (one "Cohérence" axis → two interne/externe) or
  folding into the 0201 composite → follow-up under 0201.
- Provenance and Temporality dimensions → 0201.

